n activist judge i would not say  that judge jackson earned our highest  rating well qualified for an appointment  to the supreme court now that last  remark comes from the american bar  association on thursday who lined up  with democrats in promoting judge  jackson's record as one whose decisions  that could be generational being  beneficial to both the court and the  country even though polling from earlier  this year shows the majority of  americans view the supreme court as one  that's motivated by partisanship now for  all the political posturing there's not  much republicans can do to stop  jackson's confirmation at this point  democrats can use their slim majority to  confirm her something that will cement  her place in the history books but not  change the conservative majority on the  court  jackson reggie shakini in washington  thanks reggie  next the country cutting off the crown  after a royal couple's royal backfire  queen elizabeth marked a historic  70-year reign last month now she marks a  first in the fashion world gracing the  cover of vogue magazine a young  elizabeth will be featured on a special  cover for british vogue's april issue  part of a special tribute to the  monarch's platinum jubilee  the issue arrives just weeks before she  celebrates her 96th birthday  but not everyone is celebrating the  monarchy these days especially in the  caribbean jamaica is the latest country  planning to sever ties with the  commonwealth following an earlier  decision by barbados the surprise  announcement came during a visit to the  island by prince william and the duchess  kate and as mike drollay explains their  royal tour brought back painful memories  in the former british colony  there was never a sense meeting the  jamaican prime minister would be  anything more than a photo op for the  duke and duchess of cambridge they  signed a guest book received a gift  before nodding politely as andrew  holness dropped this bombshell we are  moving on  and we i